course: dictionary
lesson: 1687
title: Chromium: the shiny metal that does not rust
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Chromium is a chemical element, which means it is a pure substance that cannot be split into anything simpler. It is a hard, shiny, silvery-grey metal, and its symbol is Cr. Its atomic number is 24.
explain: Chromium is a noun that you cannot count, so you say «some chromium», not «a chromium». In everyday talk, people often say chrome for a shiny coating of chromium on other metals.
explain: Chromium helps metal stay bright and stop rust. «That is why paint, a coat of zinc or a pinch of chromium mixed into the steel are used to keep air and water off.» Chromium is mixed with iron to make stainless steel, which does not rust.
explain: Look at the context to find the meaning. «Tiny traces of other elements, such as chromium in ruby, give corundum its colour.» The sentence says chromium is only a tiny trace, but it changes the colour of the stone, so chromium is a special ingredient, not a main part.
fact: Chromium is a chemical element with the symbol Cr and atomic number 24.
fact: Chromium is a hard, shiny, silvery-grey metal.
fact: Chromium mixed with iron makes stainless steel, which does not rust.
fact: Car parts, taps and bicycle handlebars are often chromium-plated so they shine.
fact: Chromium compounds give colour to rubies (red) and emeralds (green). Our bodies need only a very tiny amount of chromium.
exercise: «Tiny traces of other elements, such as chromium in ruby, give corundum its colour.» Which element is named as giving colour to the ruby? | Iron | Zinc | *Chromium | Water
exercise: Chromium is a hard, shiny, silvery-grey metal. What is the chemical symbol for chromium? | Cm | Chr | Ch | *Cr
exercise: Why is a pinch of chromium mixed into steel? | To turn it into glass | *To help keep air and water off, so it does not rust | To make it float on water | To make it taste sweet
test: In everyday talk, what does chrome mean? | A kind of wood used in boats | *A shiny coating of chromium put on other metals | A soft rubber used for shoes | A gas that fills balloons
test: Which sentence uses chromium correctly? | Our bodies need a chromium of tiny. | Our bodies need a very tiny chromiums. | Our bodies need a very tiny amount of chromiums. | *Our bodies need a very tiny amount of chromium.
exam: Which statement about chromium is true? | Chromium is a kind of plant that grows in ruby | Chromium is a gas that makes balloons rise | Chromium is a soft, wet liquid that floats on water | *Chromium is a hard, shiny, silvery-grey metal
